      "hints": [
        "Expand $x^2 = (-2 + \\sqrt{y + 1})^2 = y + 5 - 4(y + 1)^{1/2}$.",
        "Integrate $\\pi \\int_{-1}^3 [y + 5 - 4(y + 1)^{1/2}] dy$ from $y = -1$ to $y = 3$ to find volume $\\frac{8\\pi}{3}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Identify the $y$-limits: the lower bound is the horizontal line $y = -1$, and the upper bound is where the curve crosses the $y$-axis ($x = 0 \\implies y = 3$).",
        "Express $x^2$ in terms of $y$:\n$$x^2 = \\left(-2 + (y + 1)^{1/2}\\right)^2 = 4 - 4(y + 1)^{1/2} + (y + 1) = y + 5 - 4(y + 1)^{1/2}$$",
        "Set up and integrate the volume of revolution about the $y$-axis:\n$$V = \\pi \\int_{-1}^3 x^2\\,dy = \\pi \\int_{-1}^3 \\left(y + 5 - 4(y + 1)^{1/2}\\right) dy$$\n$$V = \\pi \\left[ \\frac{y^2}{2} + 5y - \\frac{4(y + 1)^{3/2}}{3/2} \\right]_{-1}^3 = \\pi \\left[ \\frac{y^2}{2} + 5y - \\frac{8}{3}(y + 1)^{3/2} \\right]_{-1}^3$$",
        "Evaluate at the limits $y = 3$ and $y = -1$:\n$$F(3) = \\frac{3^2}{2} + 5(3) - \\frac{8}{3}(4^{3/2}) = 4.5 + 15 - \\frac{64}{3} = \\frac{39}{2} - \\frac{64}{3} = \\frac{117 - 128}{6} = -\\frac{11}{6}$$\n$$F(-1) = \\frac{(-1)^2}{2} + 5(-1) - 0 = 0.5 - 5 = -4.5 = -\\frac{9}{2} = -\\frac{27}{6}$$\n$$V = \\pi [F(3) - F(-1)] = \\pi \\left(-\\frac{11}{6} - \\left(-\\frac{27}{6}\\right)\\right) = \\pi \\left(\\frac{16}{6}\\right) = \\frac{8\\pi}{3} \\quad (\\approx 8.38)$$"
      ],
